From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 23:54:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(cli): crowe sense reads the sensor node, direct or
 through the relay

The node and the relay serve one contract (crowe-sense/contracts/telemetry-v1.md),
so the CLI carries one resolver, endpoint(), and every subcommand goes through it:
direct mode uses the contract paths verbatim, cloud mode nests them under
/v1/nodes/{node} on the relay and carries the Crowe ID bearer.

  crowe sense use direct http://100.123.229.57:8078
  crowe sense use cloud cs-a1b2c3
  crowe sense status | latest | history --metric co2_ppm --hours 24
  crowe sense pair cs-a1b2c3 <pubkey> --zone tent-1 ; crowe sense nodes
  crowe sense check --hours 72   (runs the analysis package's sense_check.py)

No new dependencies (urllib, sqlite3, click, rich). The group's help line names
"the sensor node" rather than the product so a customer profile's --help stays
theirs; cli/commands/sense.py joins the list the branding test greps for a
hardcoded `crowe-logic login`. Tests run against a stub server that answers as
both a node and a relay.

